    "comment": "Ayyoub-inspired three-channel DJ-LGAD strip. Pitch 20 um, metal and local n++ implant width 18 um, gaps 2 um. Lateral contact windows are 0-18, 20-38, 40-58 um. Each gap has a centered 1 um wide, 1 um deep p-stop with acceptor concentration 1e13 cm^-3. The 1 um deep n++ implants are confined to the metal windows. Buried Gaussian gain layers, bulk backgrounds, and backside p+ retain the exact coefficient-version formulas. Metal width is a user-approved implementation choice, not a specified Ayyoub paper value. Geometry is 58 um by 5 mm by 50 um; 2D DEVSIM x is depth and y is lateral, both in cm. No external guard ring or oxide/interface charge is included. Frontend capacitance uses the same pitch-times-strip-length parallel-plate estimate; mutual strip capacitances are not supplied. Mesh resolves p-stop and implant edges at 0.1 um laterally and the buried gain peaks at 0.05 um in depth.",
